---
pagination:
  data: forwards
  size: 1
  alias: forward
permalink: "{{ forward.from | forwardPath }}"
layout: false
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<!doctype html>
{#- A forwarding page for an old address (content file 3.3; src/site/_data/forwards.json). GitHub Pages
    cannot send a 301, so the page sends the visitor on at once, keeping any #part of the old address
    (a person's slug), names the new page as canonical, keeps itself out of search, and shows a link
    for anyone without script. An old .php address is a folder of that name: GitHub Pages answers
    /x.php by sending the visitor to /x.php/, where this page waits. -#}
<html lang="en-IN">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>This page has moved | {{ site.name }}</title>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ site.domain }}{{ forward.to }}">
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0; url={{ forward.to }}">
<script>(function () { var to = {{ forward.to | dump | safe }}; var base = to.split('#')[0]; location.replace(location.hash ? base + location.hash : to); })();</script>
</head>
<body>
<p>This page has moved: <a href="{{ forward.to }}">{{ forward.name }}</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
